  const mode = config?.mode;
  if (typeof mode !== 'string') return false;
  const normalized = mode.trim().toLowerCase();
  return normalized === 'production' || normalized === 'prod';
}
```

The first version is usually preferable, since being strict about config values helps catch typos early. Use the lenient version only if you know you'll receive inconsistent input.

