  const result = [];
  for (const item of arr) {
    if (result.indexOf(item) === -1) result.push(item);
  }
  return result;
}
```

This is O(n²) and won't dedupe `NaN`, so prefer the `Set` version unless you're supporting very old environments.

**Note:** the function never mutates the input array — it always returns a new one.

